{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T18:47:28.570Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "lp caches by node while the value is a function of (node, seen), so on a graph with a cycle a path truncated under one caller's seen-set is reused for callers that would not have truncated. Confirmed: with edges {:d #{:c} :c #{:b} :b #{:a} :a #{:c}} the reported path for :d is [:a :b :c :d] or [:c :a :b :c :d] depending on visit order - the latter is not a path at all, it revisits :c. critical-path is unaffected because it skips cyclic nodes and walks a DAG; the draw lens is not, and it is documented as cycle-safe. Either key the memo on (node, seen), skip memoizing any result whose subtree truncated, or state that the cyclic branch returns a walk rather than a path."} :event/parents #{"sha256-163dbe14053a5e7ed97cce8e694f5be7fc93a87c42f82fb3efc96e102864a374"} :event/ticket #uuid "9b81e994-b7f5-41f6-b5bb-b7535f401864" :event/type :fact/assert}